{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1008406-how-social-are-your-solars","id":1008406,"title":"How social are your Solars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-25T21:15:48-08:00","id":1008406,"title":"How social are your Solars?","content":"So I have been mauling over First Age Exalts after an argument on the subject and I thought that I would put it here for discussion. As the title suggests the question is how social do you think Solars are? And how to portray it without putting too many of them in your game?<br /> <br /> Whether First Age or in a fairly long game it is worth considering if say Solars would seek to establish ties with each other across Creation along the lines of common interests. For example if there are only maybe ten Solars (which seems generous since that is like a 1/15th of them) that believe warstriders are the best thing ever wouldn't they try to at least to keep nominal ties? Or Twilights finding someone with a similar perspective (read:Solar Charms) and a similar field of interests?<br /> <br /> But how does one reconcile that with trying to keep the game light on the glorious golden glory-hogs so as to avoid drawing attention away from the players?<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T23:02:29-08:00","id":1008429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1008406-how-social-are-your-solars#post1008406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Twilights finding someone with a similar perspective<b> (read:Solar Charms) </b>and a similar field of interests?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's as easy as that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T23:53:23-08:00","id":1008442,"title":"","content":"This whole &quot;typecasting Solars&quot; thing seems just a touch silly to me. Really, typecasting any of the Exalted is unproductive, not that that stopped the writers of the 2e Infernals manual from trying.<br /> <br /> The Exalted of a given type have a handful of common traits that would endear them to their patron and are otherwise just as or even more diverse than any group you might come up with off the top of your head.<br /> <br /> Solars are champions, those who were faced with the impossible and went beyond it. That could mean Almost anything. In the traditional sense, it might mean coming face to face with a Behemoth as a puny mortal and punching it out, but it could also mean smooth-talking the Realm into not executing a long-hunted Anathema, or going unarmed and with no backup and intimidating an entire bandit caravan into giving up their criminal ways. In short, as social or asocial as you want.<br /> <br /> As for being social *with each other*, just depends on if they have interweavable goals and/or physical and emotional bases for friendship. And possibly reputations to approach or avoid each other on account of, they aren't Sidereals after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","name":"Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T08:47:51-08:00","id":1008561,"title":"","content":"In my game.. not at all. Frankly, the damage that five Solars can do is almost immeasurable, so I'm not about to give my PCs a bunch of Solar pen-pals. For the most part I will not acknowledge their existence. They will probably butt heads with one or two at some point who have grand designs and incompatible visions of the future, but otherwise, as far as I'm concerned, my players control the only Solars in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9749-andrew-d","name":"Andrew D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T15:18:26-08:00","id":1008691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1008406-how-social-are-your-solars#post1008406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a fairly long game it is worth considering if say Solars would seek to establish ties with each other across Creation along the lines of common interests. For example if there are only maybe ten Solars (which seems generous since that is like a 1/15th of them) that believe warstriders are the best thing ever wouldn't they try to at least to keep nominal ties? Or Twilights finding someone with a similar perspective (read:Solar Charms) and a similar field of interests?<br /> <br /> But how does one reconcile that with trying to keep the game light on the glorious golden glory-hogs so as to avoid drawing attention away from the players?<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it really depends. Some Solars will want say &quot;all Solars should work together!&quot; while others will see other Solars as rivals, and others will just take them on a case-by-case basis. And it's not just your PCs' opinions, but the NPCs' opinions, and the circumstances.<br /> I imagine that a Solar living in an area under constant threat by the Wyld Hunt is much more likely to consider other Solars natural allies and want to create some kind of pan-Solar organisation, than a Solar from a village that was destroyed by the army of the Bull of the North.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}